  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> moves on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> are fixed points, then the locus of the centroid of <math><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is a line:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VavJI",
      "text": "with slope <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vHxnJ",
      "text": "with slope <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zlwqE",
      "text": "parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UIdql",
      "text": "parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, coordinate of centroid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and coordinate of point <math><mi>P</mi></math> is <math><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>We know that the centroid of a triangle with vertices&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we have&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math> and <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></math> <math><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Since <math><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> lies on the line <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence, <math><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>For finding the locus replace&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the&nbsp;locus of centroid is <math><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> which has slope <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;since the slope of a line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
